{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1162 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "36eb07d73d75c68a96b45f7ba65c3599b55b845d4d604df08c01e69aab36c241" :edb/db-before-t 1161 :edb/db-after-t 1162 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534474 50 #inst "2026-10-07T07:16:11.015Z" 13194139534474 true] [17592186152161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290284 13194139534474 true] [17592186152162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290291 13194139534474 true] [17592186152163 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290298 13194139534474 true] [17592186152163 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290305 13194139534474 true] [17592186152340 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534474 true] [17592186152340 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/f6cbd594db6ab2454844d744ce1b776c3f561c4a6295abb9222ad2416c9f9292.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." 13194139534474 true] [17592186152340 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/q-133764.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." 13194139534474 false] [17592186152340 1145 "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,8)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(8,5).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-8}{8-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,8):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+b \\\\ 8 & =-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+b \\\\ 8 & =-1+b \\\\ 9 & =b \\\\ b & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+9.\n$$" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290284 1017 #edb/ref 17592186290285 13194139534474 true] [17592186290284 1089 "q-134002" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290284 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534474 true] [17592186290284 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/80cb125155a1a55404f2257196560a4e563e75c12d4c87c24b0464e509d7a0fa.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the trend line of the scatter plot above?" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290284 1113 #uuid "9d495c92-f887-5668-a001-304b0b353bdb" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290284 1145 "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a straight line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/18cba39701d1ec8ead1281a68fad5dab2b1f584aa396eddcfa306c4961c6397e.png)\n\nWe see that the line $s$ best fits the given data set." 13194139534474 true] [17592186290285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290286 13194139534474 true] [17592186290285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290287 13194139534474 true] [17592186290285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290288 13194139534474 true] [17592186290285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290289 13194139534474 true] [17592186290285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290290 13194139534474 true] [17592186290285 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534474 true] [17592186290285 1041 "selection" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290285 1104 #edb/ref 17592186290288 13194139534474 true] [17592186290285 1110 #uuid "d9c86b25-8508-5b27-ae3c-bf0b15f25ef2" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290286 1034 "q" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534474 true] [17592186290286 1111 #uuid "3199f78e-71f5-5d52-a8bb-857194812e28" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290287 1034 "There is no linear trend in the data" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534474 true] [17592186290287 1111 #uuid "e352ea8e-110d-5208-b2f4-db65aee1f2a3" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290288 1034 "s" 13194139534474 true] [17592186290288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186